      6 
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">تهافت</span></b>  <i>It</i> (a garment) <i>fell in pieces, piece
after piece falling off, and became worn out.</i>
(TA.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">تهافت</span> <i>It was continuous,</i> or <i>successive;</i>
syn. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">تَتَابَعَ</span>. (K.) ＝   
    <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer1"> </span>-A2-  See also 1. ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">تهافت النَّاسُ</span>
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">عَلَى المَاءِ</span> <i>The people pressed,</i> or <i>crowded, to the
water,</i> [<i>one after another,</i> or <i>party after party</i>].
(Msb.)

